  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On the AD Open Betas, I've noticed that some avatars have auto-converted bones that are completely stiff. It's like they don't have physics at all.\nThis happened on a personal avatar and the issue seems to lie with the DB stiffness settings not converting properly. \nThe dynamic bone settings are in the picture below, but it basically has a stiffness value of \"1\" with a curve to reduce stiffness throughout the chain so that the bones still move. \nThe auto-converter sets the physbones Max Angle to 0 and uses the stiffness curve for MA. This makes the bones completely stiff with no movement. \nManually increasing the Max Angle does make them move again, but it still looks incorrect because of the curve. Max Angle shouldn't be taking the curve from stiffness since MA works in reverse to stiffness. \nThe only \"fix\" was to remove the curve and set max angle to a higher value. Then the bones at least looked alright. \n The auto-converter needs to do stiffness conversion smarter or it causes issues like this. It's taking the stiffness value too directly which breaks setups because of how different max angle is to it. It also really shouldn't be taking the curve directly from stiffness.\nHere's the dynamic bones version of the personal avatar in question if you want to test the conversion for yourself. The back hair is completely stiff with AD, but moves fine with DB if you turn off the converter:\navtr_92d3abe4-545f-4495-a0d2-3c5c8f7a2ed0",
